{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,11,11]],"date-time":"2026-11-11T22:31:38Z","timestamp":1794436298265,"version":"4.9.1"},"reference-count":26,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"3","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2013,3,19]],"date-time":"2013-03-19T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1363651200000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2013,3,19]],"date-time":"2013-03-19T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1363651200000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2015,9,1]],"date-time":"2015-09-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1441065600000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":896,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["ijgo.org","elsevier.com","sciencedirect.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Intl J Gynecology &amp;amp; Obste"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2013,6]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:sec>\n                    <jats:title>Objective<\/jats:title>\n                    <jats:p>To evaluate maternal, fetal, and neonatal outcomes and their associated risk factors among pregnant women with liver cirrhosis (LC).<\/jats:p>\n                  <\/jats:sec>\n                  <jats:sec>\n                    <jats:title>Methods<\/jats:title>\n                    <jats:p>A prospective cohort study was conducted at Sohag University Hospital, Egypt, between May 1, 2009, and April 1, 2012. Participants included 129 pregnant women with LC (study group), 647 pregnant women without LC (control group 1), and 853 non\u2010pregnant women with LC (control group 2). Univariate and multivariate analyses were performed.<\/jats:p>\n                  <\/jats:sec>\n                  <jats:sec>\n                    <jats:title>Results<\/jats:title>\n                    <jats:p>\n                      Maternal, fetal, and neonatal complication rates were significantly higher in the study group than in control group 1 (\n                      <jats:italic>P<\/jats:italic>\n                      = 0.001 for all complications). The rate of hepatic decompensation (HD) was higher in the study group than in control group 2 (63.6% vs 13.6%;\n                      <jats:italic>P<\/jats:italic>\n                      = 0.001). Maternal mortality was higher in the study group (7.8%) than in either control group 1 (0.2%) or control group 2 (2.5%;\n                      <jats:italic>P<\/jats:italic>\n                      = 0.001). Variceal bleeding during vaginal delivery was the most frequent cause of maternal mortality. Vaginal delivery and increasing gestational age were the key variables affecting the rate of HD (\n                      <jats:italic>P<\/jats:italic>\n                      = 0.001 for both).\n                    <\/jats:p>\n                  <\/jats:sec>\n                  <jats:sec>\n                    <jats:title>Conclusion<\/jats:title>\n                    <jats:p>The presence of LC during pregnancy was associated with high rates of maternal and neonatal complications. Increasing gestational age and vaginal delivery were the most important risk factors for HD.<\/jats:p>\n                  <\/jats:sec>","DOI":"10.1016\/j.ijgo.2012.12.020","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2013,3,19]],"date-time":"2013-03-19T09:33:59Z","timestamp":1363685639000},"page":"247-251","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/elsevier_cm_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":51,"title":["RETRACTED: Prognosis and determinants of pregnancy outcome among patients with post\u2010hepatitis liver cirrhosis"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"121","author":[{"given":"Salah M.","family":"Rasheed","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Allam M.","family":"Abdel Monem","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Ahmed H.","family":"Abd Ellah","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mahmoud S.","family":"Abdel Fattah","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2013,3,19]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_6_2_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1111\/j.1478-3231.2009.02153.x"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_3_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1111\/j.1572-0241.2004.30231.x"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_4_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1159\/000292444"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_5_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/lt.21572"},{"issue":"3","key":"e_1_2_6_6_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"201","DOI":"10.1016\/S1665-2681(19)32011-3","article-title":"Liver cirrhosis and pregnancy","volume":"5","author":"Tiribelli C.","year":"2006","journal-title":"Ann Hepatol"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_7_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.cgh.2009.08.008"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_8_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0146-0005(98)80048-7"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_9_2","unstructured":"El\u2010ZanatyF. WayA.Egypt Demographic and Health Survey.http:\/\/www.measuredhs.com\/pubs\/pdf\/FR220\/FR220.pdf2008[Published March 2009]"},{"issue":"2","key":"e_1_2_6_10_2","first-page":"151","article-title":"Outcome of pregnancy in patients with liver cirrhosis","volume":"11","author":"Rasheed S.","year":"2007","journal-title":"Sohag Med J"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_11_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1046\/j.1365-3016.1998.00006.x"},{"issue":"9","key":"e_1_2_6_12_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1023","DOI":"10.7863\/jum.2002.21.9.1023","article-title":"Sonography of diffuse liver disease","volume":"21","author":"Tchelepi H.","year":"2002","journal-title":"J Ultrasound Med"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_13_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1259\/bjr\/75208448"},{"issue":"6","key":"e_1_2_6_14_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"899","DOI":"10.1177\/135965350701200605","article-title":"Natural history of compensated and decompensated HCV\u2010related cirrhosis in HIV\u2010infected patients: a prospective multicentre study","volume":"12","author":"Gir\u00f3n\u2010Gonz\u00e1lez J.A.","year":"2007","journal-title":"Antivir Ther"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_15_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/bjs.1800600817"},{"issue":"3","key":"e_1_2_6_16_2","first-page":"118","article-title":"Malabsorption and nutritional abnormalities in patients with liver cirrhosis","volume":"22","author":"Romiti A.","year":"1990","journal-title":"Ital J Gastroenterol"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_17_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1093\/bja\/76.2.325"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_18_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1055\/s-2000-9424"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_19_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1148\/radiology.142.2.7054836"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_20_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1111\/j.1572-0241.2001.04135.x"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_21_2","unstructured":"FontaineH. NalpasB. GilletA.Worsening of HCV\u2010related hepatitis after pregnancy. Hepatology.2000;32\u2013278A"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_22_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1097\/00006254-198205000-00002"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_23_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S1089-3261(05)70059-3"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_24_2","first-page":"979","volume-title":"Gleicher's Principles and Practice of Medical Therapy in Pregnancy","author":"Lee W.M.","year":"1991"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_25_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1111\/j.1479-828X.1999.tb03145.x"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_26_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1007\/s00404-008-0811-4"},{"key":"e_1_2_6_27_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1186\/1752-1947-1-96"}],"updated-by":[{"DOI":"10.1002\/ijgo.71505","type":"retraction","label":"Retraction","source":"publisher","